  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"2015 edition in the Artists' Publication Series from the Ringling College of Art and Design. Letterpress printed and produced at the Ringling College Letterpress and Book Arts Center."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Six french-fold structures printed on Japanese mulberry paper from photopolymer plates by Boxcar Press. Typefaces used are Humanist 521 BT, Spectrum MT, and Spindle, drawn by Ellen Knudson.--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Limited edition of 50 books, signed by the artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">French folds housed in a wrapper and clamshell enclosure.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Books are architecture -- Books are collections -- Books are environments -- Books are maps -- Books are plans -- Books are processes.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Ingress / Egress is an artists' book that contemplates the design of artists' books. The intent of the piece is to encourage ideation on the theme "books are". The six french-fold books use geometry, visual design, text, and imagery to investigate topics such as "Books are architecture", Books are collections" ... The translucency of the mulberry paper produces layers of reading in each book, and the potential of interaction of layers amongst the entire suite of books.--(Artists' statement supplied by the artist).</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="563" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Blue Dover book cloth case with Colorplan paper wrapper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
